<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I80b08b956d8e6ea0ec1e6b49ef21d005fea42e40" commit="0951ec89973797730094bbbddcd540d92ea0f60e" commit_message="devtools: Fix shopfloor_server cannot load JSON config in factory bundle.  Buildbot needs to dereference symbolic links when creating the factory.zip file, so the symlinks created in /usr/local/factory/bundle will be converted to real files.  Since shopfloor/ should be removed in future, for how we are providing a simple solution by turning symlinks into simple shell scripts.  BUG=b:64528967 TEST=emerge-eve factory;      /build/eve/usr/local/factory/bundle/shopfloor/factory_server  Change-Id: I80b08b956d8e6ea0ec1e6b49ef21d005fea42e40 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/612022 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="612022" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/22/612022/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If90898644936c4133b7dafdfb69561bbfa957d78" commit="20aadd0c51126a8763047ec9ac6ac92f89a44198" commit_message="bundle: Remove doc.zip from bundle (factory.zip).  We now publish documents on website ( https://storage.googleapis.com/chromeos-factory-docs/sdk/index.html ) so it's no longer needed to include doc.zip inside factory zip (archive, bundle).  If needed, developers can do &quot;make doc&quot; to get same documents.  BUG=None TEST=make test; emerge-eve factory  Change-Id: If90898644936c4133b7dafdfb69561bbfa957d78 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/612024 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="612024" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/24/612024/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia2991bb8ee85d94da4d0e4a0ad6629009b5477bc" commit="a8b8836c89e29071c34bb21c7bbe5a5176f0e7ae" commit_message="test list: skip tests by device data  In &lt;board&gt;_hooks.py, we used to read VPD data and check if end_SMT is set.  If end_SMT is set, then we will skip all SMT tests.  Test list `Options.skipped_tests` is extended to support this feature. For example,      options.skipped_tests = {       'device.factory.end_SMT': ['SMT']     }  The test group 'SMT' will be skipped if end_SMT is set in **device data**.  (Automatically read device data from VPD will be implemented in other CL)  The expression shares the same evaluator with FactoryTest.run_if.  So the expression can be a single python statement, with 'device' and 'constants' in your namespace.  Note that 'expr' means that, if `expr` is True, you **want** to skip those tests.  So if you want to skip LTE tests if there is no LTE devices, you should write:      options.skipped_tests = {       'not device.components.has_lte': ['*.LTE']     }  The difference between using run_if in skipped_tests and using FactoryTest.run_if is, skipped_tests will only be checked when starting Goofy.  If the device data is set later (e.g. by other pytests), rules in skipped_tests won't be triggered.  On the other hand, FactoryTest.run_if is checked every time the test is about to run.  So if device data is updated, the next test will use the latest device data to decide if it should be run or not.  The basic rule is, if the flag comes from VPD (e.g. device.factory.end_SMT), you can put it in skipped_tests.  If the value is saved in device data only, (e.g.  device.components.has_xxx), you should use FactoryTest.run_if.  BUG=b:31678190 TEST=make test  Change-Id: Ia2991bb8ee85d94da4d0e4a0ad6629009b5477bc Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/605417 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="605417" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/17/605417/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7b279233b83d45d71fc51ace15166c4c9e699787" commit="10a6a17f8bfbfb75db0cf10cc931723345aa7a77" commit_message="goofy: read device data from vpd in init_states  To make sure that device data is synced with VPD data, we often add 'read_device_data_from_vpd' to the beginning of each station.  Move this to goofy.init_states so we don't need to do it explicitly anymore. (This shouldn't break current flow, because 'write_device_data_to_vpd' should be called as soon as the device_data is updated).  Also, having this change allows us to use device data in `options.skipped_tests['&lt;expr&gt;']`.  So the logic in &lt;board&gt;_hooks.py to &quot;skip SMT tests if factory.end_SMT is set&quot; is no longer required, the new approach is:      with TestList(...) as test_list:       test_list.options.skipped_tests = {           'device.factory.end_SMT': ['SMT']           'device.factory.end_FRT': ['FRT']           'device.factory.end_RunIn': ['RunIn']       }     # or equivalent code in JSON test list.  BUG=b:31678190 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I7b279233b83d45d71fc51ace15166c4c9e699787 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/605418 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="